a flag called verbose is "-v" or "--verbose", it is a boolean.
a flag called output is "-o" or "--output", it is a text.
Parse flags.

a list called original is arguments's raw.
Print "raw length is {original's length}".
Print "count is {arguments's count}".
Print "first is {arguments's first}".
Print "second is {arguments's second}".
Print "last is {arguments's last}".
a number called firstth is 1.
a text called 'at one' is the argument at the firstth.
Print "at one is {'at one'}".
